      "updated_at": "2020-05-29T20:31:51Z",
      "body": "Though I suppose in some sense you will be able to learn this with any implementation of the event level API to some extent, especially if you configure just a single reporting window. In the existing case if a report comes T time after the last reporting window you know (% some complexity with startup scheduling) that the user hasn't started the browser for T time, so maybe this is moot.\r\n\r\nStill, I think I would be interested in seeing if this \"implicit noise\" is a problem in practice, since it does boost some of the privacy guarantees (like learning the true conversion delay).",
